      "text": "Given that the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\) are \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\), we know from Vieta's formulas that:\n\n1. \\(a + b + c = -3\\)\n2. \\(ab + bc + ca = 4\\)\n3. \\(abc = 11\\)\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(t\\) for the polynomial \\(x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0\\) whose roots are \\(a + b\\), \\(b + c\\), and \\(c + a\\).\n\nFirst, let's determine the sum of the roots of the new polynomial, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n(a + b) + (b + c) + (c + a) = 2(a + b + c)\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(a + b + c = -3\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n(a + b) + (b + c) + (c + a) = 2(-3) = -6\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time for the new polynomial. This is given by:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)(b + c) + (b + c)(c + a) + (c + a)(a + b)\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify each term individually:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)(b + c) = ab + ac + b^2 + bc\n\\]\n\\[\n(b + c)(c + a) = bc + ba + cb + ca\n\\]\n\\[\n(c + a)(a + b) = ca + ac + ab + ba\n\\]\n\nNow, let's add these together:\n\n\\[\n(ab + b^2 + ac + bc) + (bc + ba + cb + ca) + (ca + ac + ab + ba)\n\\]\n\nNotice that each term appears twice except for the diagonal terms:\n\n\\[\n2(ab + bc + ca)\n\\]\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we know that \\(ab + bc + ca = 4\\). Therefore:\n\n\\[\n2(ab + bc + ca) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate the product of the roots for the new polynomial, \\((a + b)(b + c)(c + a)\\):\n\n\\[\n(a + b)(b + c)(c + a) = abc + ab^2 + ac^2 + b^2c + bc^2 + ca^2 + a^2b + ac^2 + ab^2 = abcd + abc + ac^2 + ab^2 + bc^2 + ac^2 + b^2c + a^2b + ac^2 + ac^2 + b^3c + b^2c^2 = abc(a + b + c) + b^2c + ac^2 + bc^2\n\\]\n\nGiven \\(abc = 11\\) and \\(a + b + c = -3\\), we have:\n\n\\[\nabc(a + b + c) = 11 \\cdot (-3) = -33\n\\]\n\nNow, let's consider the remaining terms:\n\n\\[\nb^2c + ac^2 + bc^2\n\\]\n\nUsing cyclic symmetry and properties of symmetric functions, these terms will sum up to zero due to the balance of roots \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\):\n\n\\[\nb^2c + ac^2 + bc^2 = 0\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)(b + c)(c + a) = -33 + 0 = -33\n\\]\n\nCombining everything, we get:\n\n\\[\n(a + b) + (b + c) + (c + a) = -6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of the product of roots taken two at a time} = 8\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of the roots of the new polynomial} = -2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Left-hand side} = -2\n\\]\n\nTo satisfy the polynomial equation \\(x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0\\), we need to ensure the constant term \\(t\\) correctly aligns. From the polynomial identity \\(t = -(a + b)(b + c)(c + a)\\), substituting the calculated value:\n\n\\[\nt = -(-33) = 33\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(t\\) is \\(\\boxed{33}\\).",
